    <statement><p>Evaluate the function at the specified points.</p>
<p><m>f(x,y) = y+xy^{5}, \left(2,-3\right), \left(3,-1\right), \left(-5,-2\right)</m></p>
<p>At <m>\left(2,-3\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>At <m>\left(3,-1\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>At <m>\left(-5,-2\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-489</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-4</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>158</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>(x,y) = \left(2,-3\right)</m> to find 
<m>f(2,-3) = -3  + 2(-3)^{5} = -489</m>.



Similarly, with <m>(x,y) = \left(3,-1\right)</m> we find 
<m>f(3,-1) = -1  + 3(-1)^{5} = -4</m>.



Finally, for <m>(x,y) = \left(-5,-2\right)</m> we find 
<m>f(-5,-2) = -2   - 5(-2)^{5} = 158</m>.


</solution>
